---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { pageSeo } from "../../seo/registry.mjs";
import badge from "../../assets/scaling-scrum-with-scrum/ssws-badge.png";

const turnstileSiteKey = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY ?? "";
const modules = ["Pre-SSwS", "The claim", "Context-driven moves", "Five problems", "Teams of teams", "Leadership and flow", "Communication across teams", "Governance", "Reviews and planning at scale", "Transformation", "In this organization"];
const clusters = [modules.slice(0, 3), modules.slice(3, 6), modules.slice(6, 9), modules.slice(9)];
const progression = [
 ["Prerequisite", "Complete the required pre-work and let it sit for days."],
 ["Study", "Learn each module's official objectives."],
 ["Apply", "Connect the material to this organization's work."],
 ["Check", "Take an official objective-based check."],
 ["Earn SSwS", "Complete the requirements to earn the designation."],
];
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pageSeo["/training/scaling-scrum-with-scrum"]}>
<main id="main" class="ssws-page">
 <section class="ssws-hero">
  <div class="shell">
   <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">3Back</a></li><li><a href="/training">Training</a></li><li aria-current="page">Scaling Scrum with Scrum</li></ol></nav>
   <div class="hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-title"><p class="eyebrow">Scrum Leadership Series</p><h1>Scaling Scrum with Scrum</h1><p class="hero-heading">Respond at the scale the work requires.</p></div>
    <div class="hero-artifact"><Image src={badge} alt="Scaling Scrum with Scrum SSwS designation badge." width={210} height={203} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" /><p>Earn the SSwS designation.</p></div>
    <div class="hero-body"><p>Scaling is not a stamp into a large organization. It is a series of moves. Each is forced by the need to respond to demand and adjust to changing conditions. Scrum stays Scrum. It is reused as teams-of-teams. A second system is not scaling.</p><p>A short required prerequisite sits for days before the course. Then Scaling Scrum with Scrum. Private live is applied tabletop work in your structure. Public self-paced enrollment is coming soon. Complete the requirements to earn SSwS, recognized by the Scrum Guide Organization.</p><p class="quiet-line">Prerequisite required. Days before the course.</p></div>
    <div class="hero-offer"><p class="offer-line">Private live now. Public enrollment coming soon.</p><button class="enrollment" type="button" disabled>Enrollment coming soon.</button><p><a class="policy-link" href="/course-policy/">Course policies</a></p></div>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>
 <div class="proof-strip"><ul class="shell"><li>Prerequisite + 10 modules</li><li>Private live now</li><li>SSwS designation</li></ul></div>

 <section class="commercial-split section-rule"><div class="shell"><h2>Take Scaling Scrum with Scrum</h2><p class="split-lead">Same course. Two ways to take it.</p><div class="delivery-grid"><div><h3>Public self-paced</h3><p>Study the official objectives after the required prerequisite. Enrollment coming soon.</p><button class="enrollment" type="button" disabled>Enrollment coming soon.</button></div><div><h3>Private Live</h3><p>Same material, delivered to your team onsite or virtually. Applied tabletop in your structure.</p><button class="primary-cta private-request" type="button" data-private-request-trigger aria-controls="ssws-private-inquiry" aria-expanded="false">Request a private SSwS course</button><p class="private-data-sheet"><a class="policy-link" href="/training/scaling-scrum-with-scrum-data-sheet/">Read the SSwS data sheet</a></p></div></div></div></section>

 <section id="ssws-private-inquiry" class="private-inquiry" aria-labelledby="ssws-private-inquiry-title" hidden><div class="shell private-inquiry-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Private Live course inquiry</p><h2 id="ssws-private-inquiry-title">Private course conversation</h2><p>Tell us about the organization and the scaling problem. We'll reply by email to schedule a 15- to 30-minute conversation and determine whether a private onsite or virtual SSwS course is the right fit.</p></div><div><form class="private-inquiry-form" action="/api/ssws-private-inquiry" method="post" data-ssws-private-form novalidate><div class="form-fields"><div class="field"><label for="ssws-first-name">First name</label><input id="ssws-first-name" name="first_name" autocomplete="given-name" required maxlength="80" /></div><div class="field"><label for="ssws-last-name">Last name</label><input id="ssws-last-name" name="last_name" autocomplete="family-name" required maxlength="80" /></div><div class="field"><label for="ssws-email">Email</label><input id="ssws-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required maxlength="254" /></div><div class="field"><label for="ssws-confirm-email">Email again</label><input id="ssws-confirm-email" name="confirm_email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required maxlength="254" /></div><div class="field field-full"><label for="ssws-company">Company name</label><input id="ssws-company" name="company_name" autocomplete="organization" required maxlength="160" /></div><div class="field field-full"><label for="ssws-note">Tell us about the organization and the scaling problem.</label><textarea id="ssws-note" name="note" rows="5" required maxlength="4000"></textarea></div></div><div class="turnstile-wrap">{turnstileSiteKey ? <div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey={turnstileSiteKey}></div> : <p class="form-error">This form is not configured yet.</p>}</div><p id="ssws-private-form-error" class="form-error" role="alert" tabindex="-1" data-form-error hidden></p><button class="primary-cta submit-button" type="submit" disabled={!turnstileSiteKey}>Submit this request</button></form><div class="form-success" role="status" tabindex="-1" data-form-success hidden><h3>Thank you. We received your inquiry.</h3><p>We'll reply by email to schedule a 15- to 30-minute conversation about your organization and the scaling problem. Please look for our reply.</p></div></div></div></section>

 <section class="domain-guides-band"><div class="shell split"><h2>A course is not capability.</h2><div class="section-body"><p>Scaling Scrum with Scrum can give shared language and a way to see the forces. It does not develop Domain Guides. That happens in the live work of this company, with your people, over months.</p><a class="secondary-cta" href="/domain-guides">Explore the Domain Guides program</a></div></div></section>

 <section class="ssws-section section-rule"><div class="shell split"><h2>Scale without replacing Scrum</h2><div class="section-body"><p>The course gives the organization a practical account of scaling as a series of moves forced by demand and changing conditions. Structure and governance change. Scrum stays Scrum.</p><p>Through the course, you will learn to:</p><ul><li>Define scaling as a response to demand, not a target org chart</li><li>Distinguish making current teams effective from adding people first</li><li>See why installing a second system is not scaling Scrum</li><li>Treat AI as a participant in the work, not a second system. How it is used can help or hurt a scaling move.</li><li>Use Team, Pod, and Group without forcing a foreign blueprint</li><li>Decide which conversations must happen across teams, and how often</li><li>Judge a governance rule by whether it produces the right conversation at the right time</li></ul></div></div></section>

 <section class="ssws-section section-rule"><div class="shell split"><h2>Respond at the scale the work requires.</h2><div class="section-body"><p>Five problems show up when demand outgrows one team. The course names those problems and the common moves: splitting teams, adding a Product Ownership layer, centralizing for economy of scale, returning client contact, governing without a second plan.</p><p>The required prerequisite restates the scaling objectives already present in the Scrum Leadership Series. It must sit for days before the course so experience can accumulate.</p></div></div></section>

 <section class="ssws-section section-rule"><div class="shell"><h2>Demonstrate what you understand</h2><p>Work through the required prerequisite and ten course modules.</p><ol class="progression">{progression.map(([title, copy], index) => <li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></li>)}</ol></div></section>

 <section class="credential-band"><div class="shell credential-grid"><Image src={badge} alt="Scaling Scrum with Scrum SSwS designation badge." width={138} height={134} loading="lazy" /><div><p class="eyebrow">Recognition band</p><h2>Recognition based on demonstrated understanding, not attendance alone</h2><p>Earn SSwS by completing the required prerequisite and the ten course modules and passing the required objective-based checks. The designation recognizes demonstrated understanding of the Scaling Scrum with Scrum learning objectives. Completing SSwS does not say the organization can now scale. That evidence is in the work.</p><p>SSwS is recognized by the Scrum Guide Organization.</p></div></div></section>

 <section class="ssws-section section-rule"><div class="shell split"><h2>What private live includes</h2><div class="section-body"><ul><li>Applied tabletop instruction in your structure</li><li>The official Scaling Scrum with Scrum learning objectives</li><li>Official objective-based checks</li><li>The SSwS designation</li><li>Recognition through the Scrum Guide Organization</li></ul><p>The public self-paced path is the same course when it opens. Enrollment coming soon. The required prerequisite still comes first.</p></div></div></section>

 <section class="ssws-section section-rule"><div class="shell"><h2>Modules. One complete course.</h2><p>The required prerequisite plus ten modules.</p><div class="curriculum">{clusters.map((cluster, index) => <ol start={index === 0 ? 1 : clusters.slice(0, index).reduce((total, group) => total + group.length, 0) + 1}>{cluster.map(module => <li>{module}</li>)}</ol>)}</div><p><a href="/training/scaling-scrum-with-scrum/learning-objectives">Official learning objectives</a></p></div></section>

 <section class="reviews-band"><div class="shell split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Client reviews</p><h2>Coached and trained for more than 25 years.</h2></div><div class="section-body"><p>More than 25,000 people have coached and trained with 3Back.</p><a class="secondary-cta" href="/reviews/">Read 3Back reviews</a></div></div></section>

 <section class="closing-actions"><div class="shell"><h2>Choose the right course path.</h2><div class="closing-links"><button class="enrollment" type="button" disabled>Enrollment coming soon.</button><button class="primary-cta private-request" type="button" data-private-request-trigger aria-controls="ssws-private-inquiry" aria-expanded="false">Request a private SSwS course</button><a class="secondary-cta" href="/domain-guides">Explore Domain Guides</a></div></div></section>
</main>
</SiteLayout>

<script is:inline src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>
<script>
 declare global { interface Window { turnstile?: { reset(): void } } }
 const inquirySection = document.querySelector("#ssws-private-inquiry");
 const inquiryForm = document.querySelector("[data-ssws-private-form]");
 const inquiryTriggers = document.querySelectorAll('[data-private-request-trigger], a[href="#ssws-private-inquiry"]');
 if (inquirySection instanceof HTMLElement && inquiryForm instanceof HTMLFormElement) {
  const error = inquiryForm.querySelector("[data-form-error]"); const success = inquirySection.querySelector("[data-form-success]"); const button = inquiryForm.querySelector("button[type='submit']"); const firstName = inquiryForm.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[name='first_name']"); const email = inquiryForm.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[name='email']"); const confirmEmail = inquiryForm.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[name='confirm_email']");
  const focusFirstName = () => window.setTimeout(() => firstName?.focus({ preventScroll: true }), 0);
  const openInquiry = () => { inquirySection.hidden = false; inquiryTriggers.forEach((trigger) => { if (trigger.hasAttribute("aria-controls")) trigger.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "true"); }); inquirySection.scrollIntoView({ block: "start" }); focusFirstName(); };
  inquiryTriggers.forEach((trigger) => trigger.addEventListener("click", openInquiry));
  const validateEmails = () => { if (email && confirmEmail) confirmEmail.setCustomValidity(email.value && confirmEmail.value && email.value !== confirmEmail.value ? "Email addresses must match." : ""); };
  email?.addEventListener("input", validateEmails); confirmEmail?.addEventListener("input", validateEmails);
  inquiryForm.addEventListener("submit", async (event) => { event.preventDefault(); validateEmails(); if (!(error instanceof HTMLElement) || !(success instanceof HTMLElement) || !(button instanceof HTMLButtonElement)) return; error.hidden = true; inquiryForm.removeAttribute("aria-describedby"); if (!inquiryForm.reportValidity()) return; button.disabled = true; button.textContent = "Sending..."; try { const response = await fetch(inquiryForm.action, { method: "POST", body: new FormData(inquiryForm), headers: { Accept: "application/json" } }); const result = await response.json().catch(() => ({})); if (!response.ok) throw new Error(typeof result.error === "string" ? result.error : "We could not send your inquiry. Please try again."); inquiryForm.reset(); inquiryForm.hidden = true; success.hidden = false; success.focus(); } catch (submissionError) { error.textContent = submissionError instanceof Error ? submissionError.message : "We could not send your inquiry. Please try again."; error.hidden = false; inquiryForm.setAttribute("aria-describedby", error.id); error.focus(); window.turnstile?.reset(); } finally { if (!inquiryForm.hidden) { button.disabled = false; button.textContent = "Submit this request"; } } });
  if (window.location.hash === "#ssws-private-inquiry") { openInquiry(); window.addEventListener("load", focusFirstName, { once: true }); }
 }
</script>

<style>
.ssws-page { overflow-wrap: break-word; }
.ssws-hero { padding: 26px 0 44px; }
.breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 24px; font-size: .875rem; }
.breadcrumb ol { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 16px; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
.breadcrumb li + li::before { content: "/"; margin-right: 16px; color: var(--slate); }
.hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 300px; column-gap: 68px; align-items: start; }
.hero-title, .hero-body, .hero-offer { grid-column: 1; }
.eyebrow { margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--amber-text); font-weight: 700; font-size: .875rem; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
h1 { font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 3.8vw, 3.35rem); line-height: 1.12; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.hero-heading { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 20px; }
.hero-artifact { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1 / 4; align-self: center; text-align: center; }
.hero-artifact img { display: block; width: 210px; height: auto; margin-inline: auto; }
.hero-artifact p { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: .875rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.35; }
.hero-body p { margin-bottom: 16px; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.5; }
.hero-body .quiet-line { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .9375rem; font-weight: 600; }
.offer-line { margin: 6px 0 14px; font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; }
.enrollment { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 48px; padding: 11px 22px; border: 1px solid var(--slate); background: transparent; color: var(--charcoal); opacity: 1; font-weight: 700; cursor: default; }
.policy-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 4px; font-size: .875rem; font-weight: 600; }
a { text-underline-offset: 3px; }
.breadcrumb a:hover, .breadcrumb a:focus-visible, .hero-body a:hover, .hero-body a:focus-visible, .policy-link:hover, .policy-link:focus-visible { color: var(--amber-text); text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
.primary-cta, .secondary-cta { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 48px; padding: 11px 18px; font: inherit; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.25; text-align: center; text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; }
.primary-cta { border: 2px solid var(--amber); background: var(--amber); color: var(--charcoal); }
.secondary-cta { border: 1px solid currentColor; background: transparent; color: var(--charcoal); }
.primary-cta:hover, .primary-cta:focus-visible { border-color: var(--charcoal); background: var(--charcoal); color: var(--paper); }
.secondary-cta:hover, .secondary-cta:focus-visible { border-color: var(--charcoal); background: var(--charcoal); color: var(--paper); }
.proof-strip { border-block: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.proof-strip ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); list-style: none; padding-block: 21px; padding-left: 0; margin-block: 0; }
.proof-strip li { font-weight: 700; text-align: center; border-right: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.proof-strip li:last-child { border: 0; }
.private-inquiry { padding: 72px 0; scroll-margin-top: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--reading); }
.private-inquiry-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .75fr) minmax(360px, .85fr); gap: clamp(46px, 8vw, 120px); align-items: start; }
.private-inquiry-grid > div:first-child > p:last-child { max-width: 440px; font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.6; }
.private-inquiry-form { padding: clamp(26px, 4vw, 42px); border-top: 4px solid var(--amber); background: var(--paper); box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgb(29 36 33 / 8%); }
.form-fields { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; }
.field { display: grid; gap: 7px; }
.field-full { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
.field label { color: var(--charcoal); font-size: .875rem; font-weight: 700; }
.field input, .field textarea { width: 100%; padding: 12px 13px; border: 1px solid #a9ada6; border-radius: 0; background: #fff; color: var(--charcoal); font: inherit; }
.field textarea { resize: vertical; }
.turnstile-wrap { min-height: 65px; margin-top: 24px; }
.form-error { margin: 0 0 18px; color: #9e2a18; font-weight: 600; }
.submit-button { width: 100%; }
.submit-button:disabled { cursor: not-allowed; opacity: .6; }
.form-success { padding: 32px; border-top: 4px solid var(--amber); background: var(--paper); box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgb(29 36 33 / 8%); }
.form-success h3 { font-size: 1.5rem; }
.form-success p { margin-bottom: 0; }
.ssws-section { padding: 78px 0; }
h2 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3vw, 2.65rem); }
.split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr); gap: 80px; }
.section-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.section-body ul { padding-left: 22px; margin-block: 22px; }
.section-body li { margin-bottom: 12px; }
.progression { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 32px 0; border-top: 3px solid var(--amber); }
.progression li { padding: 22px 20px 10px 0; margin-right: 20px; border-right: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.progression li:last-child { border: 0; margin-right: 0; }
.step-number { display: block; color: var(--amber-text); font-size: .875rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; }
.progression h3 { font-size: 1.375rem; }
.progression p { line-height: 1.5; }
.credential-band { padding: 70px 0; background: var(--charcoal); color: var(--paper); }
.credential-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 138px minmax(0, 820px); gap: 64px; align-items: center; }
.credential-grid img { width: 138px; height: auto; }
.credential-grid h2 { max-width: 760px; }
.credential-grid p:last-child { margin: 0; }
.curriculum { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 32px; }
.curriculum ol { margin: 12px 0 0; padding: 18px 0 0 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--slate); }
.curriculum li { margin: 0 0 14px; padding-left: 4px; }
.curriculum li::marker { color: var(--amber-text); font-weight: 600; }
.commercial-split { padding: 70px 0; }
.split-lead { margin: -6px 0 30px; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; }
.delivery-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-top: 3px solid var(--amber); }
.delivery-grid > div { padding: 28px 40px 0 0; }
.delivery-grid > div + div { padding-left: 40px; border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.delivery-grid h3 { font-size: 1.45rem; }
.delivery-grid p { min-height: 72px; }
.delivery-grid .private-data-sheet { min-height: 0; margin: 20px 0 0; }
.domain-guides-band { padding: 60px 0; border-block: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--reading); }
.reviews-band { padding: 60px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.reviews-band .section-body p { font-size: 1.125rem; }
.closing-actions { padding: 76px 0; border-top: 5px solid var(--amber); background: var(--charcoal); color: var(--paper); }
.closing-actions h2 { max-width: 600px; margin-bottom: 30px; }
.closing-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; }
.closing-actions .enrollment { border-color: var(--slate); color: var(--paper); }
.closing-actions .secondary-cta { color: var(--paper); }
.closing-actions .secondary-cta:hover, .closing-actions .secondary-cta:focus-visible { border-color: var(--paper); background: var(--paper); color: var(--charcoal); }
@media (max-width: 900px) {
 .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 220px; gap: 0 30px; }
 .hero-artifact img { width: 180px; }
 .split { gap: 36px; }
 .delivery-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
 .delivery-grid > div { padding: 24px 0; }
 .delivery-grid > div + div { padding-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); border-left: 0; }
 .delivery-grid p { min-height: 0; }
 .private-inquiry-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 36px; }
 .curriculum { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
 .progression { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
 .progression li { margin: 0; padding: 18px 0; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
 .step-number { float: left; margin: 3px 20px 0 0; }
 .progression p { margin-bottom: 0; }
 .credential-grid { gap: 30px; }
}
@media (max-width: 600px) {
 .ssws-hero { padding: 18px 0 28px; }
 .breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 22px; }
 .breadcrumb ol { gap: 5px 8px; }
 .breadcrumb li + li::before { margin-right: 8px; }
 .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 112px; column-gap: 14px; }
 .hero-title { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
 h1 { font-size: 2.1rem; margin-bottom: 12px; }
 .hero-heading { font-size: 1.3rem; margin-bottom: 20px; }
 .hero-artifact { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 2; align-self: start; }
 .hero-artifact img { width: 112px; }
 .hero-artifact p { font-size: .75rem; }
 .hero-offer { grid-row: 2; }
 .hero-offer .offer-line { margin-top: 0; font-size: 1rem; }
 .hero-offer .enrollment { padding: 10px 8px; }
 .hero-body { grid-column: 1 / -1; grid-row: 3; margin-top: 24px; }
 .enrollment { width: 100%; }
 .proof-strip ul { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding-block: 8px; }
 .proof-strip li { padding: 10px 0; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
 .proof-strip li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
 .ssws-section { padding: 48px 0; }
 .split, .credential-grid, .curriculum { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; }
 .split h2 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
 .credential-band { padding: 48px 0; }
 .credential-grid img { margin-bottom: 14px; }
 .commercial-split, .domain-guides-band, .reviews-band, .closing-actions { padding: 44px 0; }
 .closing-links { display: grid; }
 .closing-links > * { width: 100%; }
 .form-fields { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
 .field-full { grid-column: auto; }
}
</style>
